0,1]$ is closed, but the function is not continuous on it because it is not defined at $x=0$ (it makes zero the denominator).   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval  $[0,1)$   is not closed, so the extreme value theorem is not applicable.\n\n- The interval $[-2,-1]$    is closed, and the function is continuous on $[-2,-1].$   Therefore, the extreme value theorem is applicable.\n\nIn conclusion, the correct answer is $[-2,-1]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186175901 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eede91c4-9099-55df-a803-f87895d9f51b" :knowledge-point/title "Applying the Extreme Value Theorem to Piecewise Functions" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048748 :topic/id #uuid "bad1cfe2-7639-5714-8417-2b8af7ece5cb" :topic/math-academy-id 3571 :topic/title "The Extreme Value Theorem"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61d52bbf-27b3-5866-b828-58197f11fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468040} {:answer/id #uuid "c05f5724-e978-5eea-b92e-be4ff7cc5a0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61d52bbf-27b3-5866-b828-58197f11fac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468040} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc14219f-7f18-5ba0-9fb0-e04cfae28cad" :answer-field/key "$[-1,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468741} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5693a553-a140-59da-b649-fed8ae8eea18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468042} {:answer/id #uuid "5d98483c-577a-5658-83b7-1140163