nswer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12bceb91-74c2-5e73-9356-37da01924e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468189} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0ef2716-8518-50cd-b34e-ca5d64fce6a3" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (4,6)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468815}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a8275053-44d7-522b-8662-3358231e9c18" :question/math-academy-id "q-76218" :question/problem "![](images/18/186ac941080da34b7c149534a2e255852241b28855c0ef15db2beee2d692007a.png)\n\nConsider the function $y=f(x)$ above. On which of the following intervals is the function continuous? \n\nYou may assume that all points of discontinuity of $f(x)$ are shown in the diagram.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each statement.\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,3].$ Although the function is continuous on $(-\\infty ,3),$ it is not left-continuous at $x=3.$\n\n- The function is *not* continuous on $(-\\infty ,5)$ because it contains a discontinuity at $x=3.$\n\n- The function is continuous on $(4,6).$ It is continuous on $[3,\\infty )$ and this contains the interval $(4,6).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in (4,6)$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345292 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096691 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c015dcaa-2155-5d80-985b-21924de92b28" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Vector Equalities" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050467 :topic/id #uuid "4bf7862e-8b34-577f-9a7c-1f3cc4989b50" :topic/math-academy-id 1102 :topic/title "Problem Solving Using Vector Diagrams"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ee64b11-50e3-58bf-941c-0b764a47e996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468190} {:answer/id #uuid "b535810e-56e1-5a05-91bf-f35a40249c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b535810e-56e1-5a05-91bf-f35a40249c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468191} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1edde74-0e7d-5c48-99ec-7e8fffb51a33" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468816} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b10e04d-2538-51fb-bb14-fb2259044599" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468192} {:answer/id #uuid "4c56a456-470e-576d-9050-ca50151f219e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c56a456-470e-576d-9050-ca50151f219e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468193} :answer-field/id #uuid "fde356fb-9367-5ccd-b831-7c6803cc9c06" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468817} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32549e3f-1dea-5872-bfc1-9beea9403807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468194} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d0b92a-e970-5a2a-831a-9f1b79448351" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32549e3f-1dea-5872-bfc1-9beea9403807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468194} :answer-field/id #uuid "25370d92-c63f-5b70-9799-ef868455aca1" :answer-field/key "$\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468818}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "43864da8-ac06-5dee-a580-c31c2739a8e7" :question/math-academy-id "q-77389" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e17584d96cb8d83ccb1abfbd16c4117f58639b7cd3462ee50ad3f31e4eabe279.png)\n\nIn figure $ABCDEF$ shown above, which of the following equalities are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{BC}+\\overset{\\to }{CD} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BD}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$ is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+(\\overset{\\to }{AE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}) \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{BF}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Equality $\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{FC}$ is false. Indeed,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}-\\overset{\\to }{ED}-\\overset{\\to }{FE} & =(\\overset{\\to }{CD}+\\overset{\\to }{DE})+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{CF} \\\\  & \\ne \\overset{\\to }{FC}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $\\overset{\\to }{BC}-\\overset{\\to }{DC}=\\overset{\\to }{BD}$; $\\overset{\\to }{BA}+\\overset{\\to }{AE}-\\overset{\\to }{FE}=\\overset{\\to }{BF}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050129 :topic/id #uuid "2eee4710-3f26-5186-948b-a819cfaf4083" :topic/math-academy-id 1775 :topic/title "Cramer's Rule for 2x2 Systems of Linear Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7a2c945-cc7a-516f-b667-0d89251d3b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468196} {:answer/id #uuid "40dd3909-7386-578c-83fe-14ada120188c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40dd3909-7386-578c-83fe-14ada120188c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197} :answer-field/id #uuid "a689391a-097b-5af2-9f28-47cb333ebeda" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-6$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7b34da-0847-5b45-af70-c9c06b31eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} {:answer/id #uuid "a7025902-02fe-5c8c-8871-b5a8b672cf56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd7b34da-0847-5b45-af70-c9c06b31eade" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} :answer-field/id #uuid "55fe37fb-e330-5dc6-9f1e-3cb5a382485e" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-12$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f36311c-d5c2-569b-97ab-eaf35ae46749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} {:answer/id #uuid "4903bf3a-5ec0-502a-9315-987f705aa1f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f36311c-d5c2-569b-97ab-eaf35ae46749" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa69594-ec70-57b1-b89f-3696a43adfec" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=3$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468821}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dfe3c702-6424-5bb5-8a56-52b5a6e22724" :question/math-academy-id "q-77400" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|}{3} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-6$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345294 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119790 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bd9b0f65-d8a3-57c4-88c5-2738b0938c0d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050129 :topic/id #uuid "2eee4710-3f26-5186-948b-a819cfaf4083" :topic/math-academy-id 1775 :topic/title "Cramer's Rule for 2x2 Systems of Linear Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d68061f9-26f7-5cb1-b451-9613d07f582b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} {:answer/id #uuid "305d62c3-fb2c-554a-888b-993e673cc358" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d68061f9-26f7-5cb1-b451-9613d07f582b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7204a3ea-ab6b-5c40-bbe8-ec855216acb2" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=5$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29506dd5-d859-5ad5-9d4b-430345bd390d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa20fab-5c90-5c84-a527-307ae07a2504" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29506dd5-d859-5ad5-9d4b-430345bd390d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae3e59d-3a9b-58cd-9548-f87659ec9274" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db9a7f34-a705-56e4-95cf-26717aba6aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468206} {:answer/id #uuid "b87a5642-b55a-55d3-b69c-559ebce5dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b87a5642-b55a-55d3-b69c-559ebce5dc2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207} :answer-field/id #uuid "f473da0d-0013-52fe-bd69-e5c67cc3e1ac" :answer-field/key "$|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a75a54e5-59f0-5536-9005-ac12974e1a69" :question/math-academy-id "q-77401" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,1⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=k \\\\ x+4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dbedfadc-d9f9-52d0-bbba-03edb6bc60ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438538} {:answer/id #uuid "5d43d60c-3622-599a-8b85-3c1e1a43bcbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5d43d60c-3622-599a-8b85-3c1e1a43bcbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438539} :answer-field/id #uuid "a785d799-8f86-537c-9118-e054fcef0a8b" :answer-field/key "$S$ is **not** a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439298} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c9d8d50-586f-5771-9f5d-c653bddf834f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438540} {:answer/id #uuid "42f92594-420e-56b2-8230-647afe1c9aaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c9d8d50-586f-5771-9f5d-c653bddf834f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438540} :answer-field/id #uuid "d867bc0f-f70b-585f-a45f-e93f7009ccc2" :answer-field/key "$S$ is a singular matrix" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439299} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18ff0d6c-b87c-5984-8531-3ab4593d5874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438542} {:answer/id #uuid "f7d7a091-3679-5176-83a5-c487d3076d00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438543}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18ff0d6c-b87c-5984-8531-3ab4593d5874" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438542} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ed5cd0c-b4fb-5dc7-b022-c94731ea1ca5" :answer-field/key "$det(S)=\\sqrt{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439300}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a70a69db-90d3-5dde-88c1-3f25b19af419" :question/math-academy-id "q-77477" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $S$ given below?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$$\nS=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & \\,0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\,\\,-1 \\\\ 4 & \\,\\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\,-1 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & \\,-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(-{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}+4)-2(-2\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{3})+0 \\\\  & =(-3+4)-2\\cdot (-\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =1+2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=1+2\\sqrt{3}\\ne 0$, the matrix is **not ** singular. \n\nTherefore, only statement “$S$ is **not** a singular matrix” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "32df8909-a239-5167-b8ea-412f7cdaea93" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Singular Matrices" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048146 :topic/id #uuid "832923c0-f0e3-599f-af85-37cb7dae2658" :topic/math-academy-id 153 :topic/title "The Determinant of a 3x3 Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b334514-5ffc-51e3-97fb-0f2d53233c1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438544} {:answer/id #uuid "18f72f9f-a4e0-5a07-bd3b-f673eb247d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438545}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18f72f9f-a4e0-5a07-bd3b-f673eb247d5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" 