:answer/id #uuid "1721e2cd-1c3a-5cf8-a293-7ba1b2112a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451710} :answer-field/id #uuid "88140b3a-d029-5345-baf0-7023275454a2" :answer-field/key "$D={B}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452702}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a09e0ac-b938-5176-9b09-5c3e47da17ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-7907" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{15} & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{3}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $BC=CB={I}_{3}$ is false.\n\n- Note, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{3}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $BD=DB={I}_{3}$ is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement $D={B}^{-1}$ is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $BD=DB={I}_{3}$; $D={B}^{-1}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348162 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087700 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a75c67e5-3469-5730-9181-54df4ec6d5b2" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a Larger Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049125 :topic/id #uuid "dcaddd67-a2eb-5a06-88ab-be47014dbd14" :topic/math-academy-id 863 :topic/title "Introduction to the Inverse of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df2e0d17-fa3f-5143-a321-2a068c4e955c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451711} {:answer/id #uuid "f34b5bc1-f3f2-51e7-9aea-110521bf1ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451712}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df2e0d17-fa3f-5143-a321-2a068c4e955c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451711} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff75d4bf-5306-5a64-b21f-bcf8026e0f99" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "99337b17-8708-5107-bfbe-9e15d078c7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451713} {:answer/id #uuid "0a3e55a7-7e53-5335-93d5-f72501ec6ca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451714}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99337b17-8708-5107-